NAME
       fsadm - grow the file system on a device to fill it (used by lvextend -r)

SYNOPSIS
       fsadm resize DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       fsadm is a helper from the LVM tools. fsadm resize DEVICE makes the
       file system on DEVICE (xfs, ext4) as big as the device: it runs
       xfs_growfs or resize2fs for you. lvextend -r (--resizefs) and
       lvresize -r call it after making the logical volume bigger, which is
       why one command can grow both.

EXAMPLES
       Grow a logical volume by 500 MiB together with its file system:

           lvextend -r -L +500M /dev/vgdata/lvdata

       Grow the file system by hand after a plain lvextend:

           fsadm resize /dev/vgdata/lvdata

SEE ALSO
       lvextend(8), xfs_growfs(8), resize2fs(8)
